Support: getMainExecutable() must not return "" when /proc/self/exe exists
but cannot be read.

What: retry readlink a few times, then fall through to the argv[0]-based
detection that is already used when /proc is absent.
Why: on iSH the readlink fails intermittently; clang, lld and swift-frontend then
could not find their resource directory, config file or ld.lld.
Upstream: reasonable hardening, likely acceptable.

Apply inside the `llvm-project` repository: git apply <this file>
---
diff --git a/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc b/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
--- a/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
+++ b/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
@@ -254,10 +254,13 @@
   const char *aPath = "/proc/self/exe";
   if (sys::fs::exists(aPath)) {
     // /proc is not always mounted under Linux (chroot for example).
-    ssize_t len = ::readlink(aPath, exe_path, sizeof(exe_path));
-    if (len < 0)
-      return "";
-
+    // The read can fail spuriously in some environments (sandboxes, emulators
+    // such as iSH), so retry a few times and otherwise fall back to the
+    // classical argv[0] based detection below instead of giving up.
+    ssize_t len = -1;
+    for (unsigned Attempt = 0; Attempt < 8 && len < 0; ++Attempt)
+      len = ::readlink(aPath, exe_path, sizeof(exe_path));
+    if (len >= 0) {
     // Null terminate the string for realpath. readlink never null
     // terminates its output.
     len = std::min(len, ssize_t(sizeof(exe_path) - 1));
@@ -278,6 +281,7 @@
     if (realpath(exe_path, real_path))
       return std::string(real_path);
 #endif
+    }
   }
   // Fall back to the classical detection.
   if (getprogpath(exe_path, argv0))
